                "senderName": "NWS Anchorage AK",
                "headline": "Winter Weather Advisory issued November 12 at 9:44AM AKST until November 13 at 6:00PM AKST by NWS Anchorage AK",
                "description": "* WHAT...Snow and mixed precipitation expected. Total snow\naccumulations from 2 to 10 inches.\n\n* WHERE...Kodiak Island Northeast.\n\n* WHEN...From 6 PM this evening to 6 PM AKST Friday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Heavy snow and rain on snow may create difficult travel\nconditions.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...A compact storm will move southeast of Kodiak\nIsland tonight and remain nearly stationary through Friday\nafternoon to evening. Slight deviations in the storm position to\nthe east and west will cause snow levels to fluctuate between sea\nlevel and 400 ft in elevation. Kodiak city and the archipeligo to\nthe north are most likely to mix with rain at times, resulting in\ntotal snow accumulations of 2 to 4 inches. If rain does not mix in,\nexpect higher snow totals. Areas from Kodiak Airport to Women's Bay\nare more likely to maintain a northwest wind, resulting in colder\ntemperatures, a lower likelihood of rain, and snow accumulations\nfrom 6 to 10 inches.",
                "instruction": "Slow down and use caution while traveling. For the latest road\nconditions call 5 1 1 or visit 511.alaska.gov.",
